    {
      "page_idx": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.322,
            0.065,
            0.677,
            0.123
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Outline and Assumptions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.177,
            0.485,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": "I’ll briefly summarize the following sections:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.233,
            0.339,
            0.275
          ],
          "content": "4.1 Learning Heuristics"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.289,
            0.433,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": "4.2. Learning Action Specifications"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.345,
            0.43,
            0.387
          ],
          "content": "4.2.2 Online Action Learning"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.101,
            0.511,
            0.399,
            0.554
          ],
          "content": "● Classical planning assumptions:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.567,
            0.468,
            0.609
          ],
          "content": "• Finite, static world, just one actor"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.623,
            0.513,
            0.664
          ],
          "content": "• No concurrent actions, no explicit time"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.679,
            0.427,
            0.72
          ],
          "content": "Determinism, no uncertainty"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.734,
            0.613,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": "• Sequence of states and actions $\\langle s _ { 0 } , a _ { 1 } , s _ { 1 } , a _ { 2 } , s _ { 2 } , \\ldots \\rangle$"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.006,
            0.975,
            0.355,
            0.997
          ],
          "content": "Lecture slides for [Acting, Planning, and Learning](https://projects.laas.fr/planning/). Creative Commons [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en)"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.984,
            0.976,
            0.994,
            0.994
          ],
          "content": "2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.335,
            0.066,
            0.663,
            0.123
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "4.1. Learning Heuristics"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.054,
            0.177,
            0.202,
            0.218
          ],
          "content": "\\mathsf {L R T A} ^ {*} (\\Sigma , s _ {0}, S _ {g}, h _ {0})",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.079,
            0.225,
            0.486,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": "$s \\gets s _ { 0 } ; \\; \\pi \\gets \\big \\langle \\big \\rangle$ // initialize current state and plan $h ( s ) \\leftarrow h _ { 0 } ( s )$ for every s∈ S // initialize the heuristic **while** $s \\notin S _ { g }$ **do**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.367,
            0.346,
            0.407
          ],
          "content": "**for each** a in Applicable(s) **do**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.413,
            0.367,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": "Q (s, a) \\leftarrow \\mathrm{cost} (s, a) + h (\\gamma (s, a))",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.461,
            0.259,
            0.503
          ],
          "content": "h (s) \\leftarrow \\min _ {a} Q (s, a)",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.51,
            0.265,
            0.551
          ],
          "content": "a \\leftarrow \\operatorname{argmin} _ {a} Q (s, a)",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.563,
            0.188,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": "\\pi \\leftarrow \\pi \\cdot a",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.605,
            0.194,
            0.645
          ],
          "content": "s \\leftarrow \\gamma (s, a)",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.512,
            0.177,
            0.842,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": "● Assume the domain is safely explorable"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.543,
            0.229,
            0.836,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": "▸ At every state s there is a path to $S _ { g }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.512,
            0.28,
            0.939,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": "● In each state $s ,   Q ( s , a )$ is the estimated cost of getting to $S _ { g }$ if we start with action a"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.369,
            0.782,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": "● $\\mathsf { L R T A ^ { * } }$ finds a path from $s _ { 0 }$ to $S _ { g }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.543,
            0.42,
            0.862,
            0.462
          ],
          "content": "▸ Updates $h ( s )$ for every s along the path"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.471,
            0.921,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": "● Call it again, it finds another path, updates h along that path"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.563,
            0.891,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": "● After enough calls, it will find an optimal path"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.543,
            0.615,
            0.784,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": "▸ Along that path, $h ( s ) = h ^ { * } ( s )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.544,
            0.666,
            0.76,
            0.705
          ],
          "content": "▸ But not along other paths"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.769,
            0.933,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": "● Other algorithms to find a heuristic h that is close to $h ^ { * }$ at every state"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.544,
            0.861,
            0.754,
            0.897
          ],
          "content": "▸ Based on value iteration"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.006,
            0.975,
            0.354,
            0.997
          ],
          "content": "Lecture slides for [Acting, Planning, and Learning](https://projects.laas.fr/planning/). Creative Commons [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en)"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.985,
            0.975,
            0.994,
            0.995
          ],
          "content": "3"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 3,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.259,
            0.065,
            0.739,
            0.124
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "4.2. Learning Action Specifications"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.053,
            0.187,
            0.503,
            0.226
          ],
          "content": "● Action trace: a triple (s, head(a), s′) such that $\\gamma ( s , a ) = s ^ { \\prime }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.238,
            0.441,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": "▸ $( \\{ \\mathsf { l o c } ( \\mathsf { r } 1 ) = \\mathsf { d } 3 , \\mathsf { c a r g o } ( \\mathsf { r } 1 ) = \\mathsf { r i } 1 , \\mathsf { l o c } ( \\mathsf { c } 1 ) = \\mathsf { d } 1 \\} ,$ $\\mathsf { m o v e } ( \\mathsf { r 1 } , \\mathsf { d 3 } , \\mathsf { d 1 } ) ,$ $\\{ \\mathsf { l o c } ( \\mathsf { r } 1 ) = \\mathsf { d } 1 , \\mathsf { c a r g o } ( \\mathsf { r } 1 ) = \\mathsf { r i l } , \\mathsf { l o c } ( \\mathsf { c } 1 ) = \\mathsf { d } 1 \\} )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.054,
            0.397,
            0.337,
            0.433
          ],
          "content": "Let Σ be a state-transition system,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.105,
            0.437,
            0.391,
            0.477
          ],
          "content": "$T _ { \\Sigma } = \\{ \\mathrm { a l l }$ possible action traces for $\\sum \\gamma$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.054,
            0.515,
            0.325,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": "● Action model learning problem:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.565,
            0.373,
            0.603
          ],
          "content": "▸ Given a set of action traces $T \\subseteq T _ { \\Sigma }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.617,
            0.382,
            0.655
          ],
          "content": "examples of what the actions do"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.665,
            0.498,
            0.703
          ],
          "content": "▸ Create an action model $\\mathcal { A M } = ( X _ { } { s y m } , A _ { } { s y m } , S _ { } { c h e m a } )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.719,
            0.497,
            0.798
          ],
          "content": "Xsym and Asym are sets of state-variable names and action names (without arguments)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.809,
            0.463,
            0.888
          ],
          "content": "Schema is a function that maps each action name α ∈ Asym into an action schema"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.535,
            0.185,
            0.858,
            0.223
          ],
          "content": "● AM defines a state-transition system $\\Sigma ^ { \\prime }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.536,
            0.238,
            0.883,
            0.279
          ],
          "content": "● Let $T _ { \\Sigma ^ { \\prime } } = \\{ \\mathrm { a l l }$ possible action traces for $\\Sigma ^ { \\prime } \\}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.536,
            0.327,
            0.743,
            0.367
          ],
          "content": "● $\\mathcal { A } \\mathcal { M }$ is sound if $T _ { \\Sigma ^ { \\prime } } \\subseteq T _ { \\Sigma }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.566,
            0.381,
            0.937,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": "▸ $T _ { \\Sigma ^ { \\prime } }$ doesn’t include any incorrect action traces"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.536,
            0.429,
            0.765,
            0.469
          ],
          "content": "● AM is complete if $T _ { \\Sigma } \\subseteq T _ { \\Sigma ^ { \\prime } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.567,
            0.483,
            0.877,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": "$T _ { \\Sigma ^ { \\prime } }$ includes every correct action trace"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.536,
            0.574,
            0.816,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": "● Three ways to get the traces in T:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.567,
            0.625,
            0.645,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": "▸ offline"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.567,
            0.677,
            0.642,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": "▸ online"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.567,
            0.727,
            0.786,
            0.765
          ],
          "content": "▸ from “informative states”"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.006,
            0.975,
            0.354,
            0.997
          ],
          "content": "Lecture slides for [Acting, Planning, and Learning](https://projects.laas.fr/planning/). Creative Commons [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en)"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.985,
            0.977,
            0.994,
            0.993
          ],
          "content": "4"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 4,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.334,
            0.065,
            0.665,
            0.123
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Three Kinds of Learning"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.055,
            0.178,
            0.21,
            0.217
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "● Offline learning:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.229,
            0.416,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": "▸ Given a fixed set of action traces $T \\subseteq T _ { \\Sigma }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.281,
            0.393,
            0.32
          ],
          "content": "▸ Advantage: quick access to examples"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.331,
            0.45,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": "Disadvantage: The examples might not show you conclusively what each action does"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.054,
            0.449,
            0.466,
            0.489
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Online learning: learner generates T by acting in Σ"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.5,
            0.458,
            0.62
          ],
          "content": "▸ Observe current state, choose action a, send it to the execution platform, see what state it produces, …"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.631,
            0.465,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": "▸ Advantage: If you’re unsure what a does in the current state, you can try it and see"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.722,
            0.466,
            0.839
          ],
          "content": "▸ Disadvantage: Each action execution takes time. Collecting enough observations may take lots of time."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.178,
            0.796,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": "● Learning from informative states:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.544,
            0.229,
            0.864,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": "▸ Suppose the learner has an oracle for Σ"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.569,
            0.282,
            0.767,
            0.32
          ],
          "content": "• e.g., a quick simulator"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.544,
            0.331,
            0.93,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": "Given (s,a), it either returns γ(s,a) or says that a isn’t applicable"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.544,
            0.422,
            0.926,
            0.499
          ],
          "content": "▸ Advantage: Learner can try a in many different states until it’s sure what a does"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.544,
            0.514,
            0.912,
            0.591
          ],
          "content": "▸ Disadvantage: Not feasible unless you have a simulator that’s both fast and accurate"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.643,
            0.903,
            0.721
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "In all three cases, observations give information about actions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.543,
            0.737,
            0.866,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": "▸ To get action schemas, must generalize"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.543,
            0.787,
            0.807,
            0.825
          ],
          "content": "▸ Use techniques based on lifting"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.006,
            0.975,
            0.354,
            0.997
          ],
          "content": "Lecture slides for [Acting, Planning, and Learning](https://projects.laas.fr/planning/). Creative Commons [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en)"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.984,
            0.976,
            0.994,
            0.995
          ],
          "content": "5"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.279,
            0.065,
            0.721,
            0.119
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Lifted Preconditions and Effects"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.054,
            0.177,
            0.385,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": "● Recall what an action schema looks like"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.229,
            0.28,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": "▸ head: $n a m e ( z _ { 1 } ,   \\dots ,   z _ { n } )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.281,
            0.471,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": "pre: atoms in which every object variable is one of $[ z _ { 1 } , \\dots , z _ { n }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.37,
            0.483,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": "eff: assignments in which every object variable is one of $[ z _ { 1 } , \\dots , z _ { n }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.053,
            0.503,
            0.449,
            0.541
          ],
          "content": "● Assume the action schemas contain no constants"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.551,
            0.41,
            0.591
          ],
          "content": "▸ Then the action schemas are fully lifted"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.604,
            0.218,
            0.643
          ],
          "content": "▸ In pre and eff,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.656,
            0.481,
            0.735
          ],
          "content": "• every state variable contains only $z _ { 1 } ,   . . . ,   z _ { n }   { \\mathfrak { a } } { \\mathfrak { s } }$ parameters"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.748,
            0.484,
            0.787
          ],
          "content": "• every state variable’s value is one of $[ z _ { 1 } , . . . , z _ { n }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.512,
            0.177,
            0.924,
            0.271
          ],
          "continues_prev": true,
          "content": "● Suppose we’re given an action trace $( \\{ \\mathsf { l o c } ( \\mathsf { r } 1 ) = \\mathsf { d } 3 \\} , \\mathsf { m o v e } ( \\mathsf { r } 1 , \\mathsf { d } 3 , \\mathsf { d } 1 ) ,   \\{ \\mathsf { l o c } ( \\mathsf { r } 1 ) = \\mathsf { d } 1 \\} )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.28,
            0.927,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": "● We want to figure out the preconditions and effects of move $( z _ { 1 } , z _ { 2 } , z _ { 3 } )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.371,
            0.837,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": "● For pre and eff, consider atoms such as lo $\\mathtt { c } ( z _ { 1 } ) = z _ { 2 } ,   \\mathsf { I o c } ( z _ { 1 } ) = z _ { 3 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "bbox": [
            0.52,
            0.617,
            0.961,
            0.846
          ],
          "sub_type": "code",
          "content": "```txt\nThis restriction can exclude useful action schemas, e.g.\n    load(r, c, l)\n        pre: cargo(r)=nil, loc(c)=l, loc(r)=l\n        eff: cargo(r)←c, loc(c)←r\n```",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": []
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.006,
            0.975,
            0.354,
            0.997
          ],
          "content": "Lecture slides for [Acting, Planning, and Learning](https://projects.laas.fr/planning/). Creative Commons [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en)"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.985,
            0.976,
            0.994,
            0.994
          ],
          "content": "6"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 6,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.303,
            0.065,
            0.695,
            0.124
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Offline Learning (Basic Idea)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.053,
            0.177,
            0.461,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": "● Given $T \\subseteq T _ { \\Sigma } \\mathrm { ~ - ~ }$ a set of triples $( s , \\alpha ( \\mathbf { c } _ { 1 } , \\ldots , \\mathbf { c } _ { k } ) , s ^ { \\prime } )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.053,
            0.255,
            0.471,
            0.294
          ],
          "content": "For each α, begin with action schema (head,pre,eff)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.307,
            0.245,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": "$h e a d = \\alpha ( z _ { 1 } { , } { \\cdots } { , } z _ { k } )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.359,
            0.458,
            0.437
          ],
          "content": "▸ $p r e =$ {atoms of the form $x ( z ^ { \\prime } { } _ { 1 } , \\ldots , z ^ { \\prime } { } _ { n } ) = z ^ { \\prime } { } _ { n + 1 }$ where x ∈ Xsym and each ${ \\boldsymbol { z } } ^ { \\prime } { } _ { i }$ is one of $\\scriptstyle z _ { 1 } , \\ldots , z _ { k } \\}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.087,
            0.447,
            0.163,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": "▸ $e f f = \\emptyset$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.054,
            0.499,
            0.342,
            0.537
          ],
          "content": "● **for** every $( s , \\alpha ( c _ { 1 } , . . . , c _ { k } ) , s ^ { \\prime } ) \\in T$ **do**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.551,
            0.43,
            0.667
          ],
          "content": "▸ **for** every atom $x ( z _ { 1 } ^ { \\prime } , \\ldots , z _ { n } ^ { \\prime } ) = z _ { n + 1 } ^ { \\prime }$ in pre $( \\alpha ( z _ { 1 } , { \\ldots } , z _ { k } ) )$ that doesn’t have a ground instance in s **do**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.683,
            0.37,
            0.721
          ],
          "content": "• remove it from $\\operatorname { p r e } ( \\alpha ( z _ { 1 } { , } { \\cdots } { , } z _ { k } ) )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.733,
            0.433,
            0.812
          ],
          "content": "▸ **for** every atom $x ( z _ { 1 } , \\ldots , z _ { n } ) = z _ { n + 1 }$ that has a ground instance in $s ^ { \\prime } \\setminus s$ **do**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.826,
            0.432,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": "• add $x ( z _ { 1 } , \\ldots , z _ { n } ) \\longleftarrow z _ { n + 1 }$ to $\\mathbf { e f f } ( \\alpha ( z _ { 1 } { , \\ldots , } z _ { k } )$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.512,
            0.177,
            0.825,
            0.214
          ],
          "content": "● Need to fill in some additional details"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.512,
            0.229,
            0.872,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": "● Can prove it produces a sound action model"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.543,
            0.279,
            0.633,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": "▸ $T _ { \\Sigma ^ { \\prime } } \\subseteq T _ { \\Sigma }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.512,
            0.33,
            0.943,
            0.409
          ],
          "content": "● Completeness depends on whether T contains enough action traces"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.421,
            0.937,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": "● Can enhance the algorithm by allowing action traces of the form"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.543,
            0.514,
            0.78,
            0.553
          ],
          "content": "$( s , \\alpha ( \\mathbf { c } _ { 1 } { , \\ldots , } c _ { k } ) ,$ , inapplicable)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.615,
            0.858,
            0.655
          ],
          "content": "● As given, the algorithm is very inefficient"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.543,
            0.666,
            0.924,
            0.745
          ],
          "content": "▸ each action schema starts with huge number of preconditions, must remove most of them"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.759,
            0.875,
            0.795
          ],
          "content": "● Paolo will revise it to make it more efficient"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.006,
            0.975,
            0.354,
            0.997
          ],
          "content": "Lecture slides for [Acting, Planning, and Learning](https://projects.laas.fr/planning/). Creative Commons [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en)"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.985,
            0.976,
            0.994,
            0.994
          ],
          "content": "7"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_idx": 7,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.349,
            0.066,
            0.65,
            0.123
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "4.2.2 Online Learning"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.054,
            0.191,
            0.315,
            0.233
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "● Learning actions by queries"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.085,
            0.247,
            0.468,
            0.287
          ],
          "content": "▸ Access to an oracle, e.g., a quick simulator"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.303,
            0.255,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": "▸ Informative state"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.357,
            0.45,
            0.441
          ],
          "content": "• A state s such that γ(s,a) will provide needed information about a"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.457,
            0.4,
            0.497
          ],
          "content": "Generate queries about such states"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.513,
            0.465,
            0.598
          ],
          "content": "Can write an algorithm that is both correct and complete"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.513,
            0.191,
            0.729,
            0.232
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "● Online action learning"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.545,
            0.247,
            0.939,
            0.377
          ],
          "content": "▸ Observe current state, choose action a, send it to the execution platform, see what state it produces, …"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.545,
            0.391,
            0.882,
            0.474
          ],
          "content": "▸ Try to generate plans that will lead to informative states"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.006,
            0.975,
            0.354,
            0.997
          ],
          "content": "Lecture slides for [Acting, Planning, and Learning](https://projects.laas.fr/planning/). Creative Commons [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en)"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
